    description: "Two Dart constructor gaps, found by PR 5 agent 2 (WI-haloz):\n\n1. A Dart constructor's stable id hashes no parameter list, only the owner-qualified name (WI-tusad's design). So the names of named parameters (`this.x`, `super.x`, typed named parameters) enter no id. PR 5 hashes named-parameter names for functions and methods only.\n   - Owner question: should a constructor hash its parameter list (with named-parameter labels, as functions and methods now do)? This would be a policy change that moves every Dart constructor id with parameters.\n2. Factory constructors emit no symbol at all. Repro: `class W { factory W.make({required int count}) => W._(); W._(); }` produces no symbol for `W.make`.\n\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/haloz/RESULTS.md."  # a017
